  "description": "A creative software challenge where teams build quirky, unusual, and entertaining software rather than traditional corporate tools. Participants must combine unconventional UX, technical absurdity, and creative engineering to build prototypes that surprise, amuse, and captivate the jury. Rules: Teams must consist of 1 to 4 members . Software must focus on entertainment, absurdity, and quirky creativity rather than enterprise utilities. All code must be authored within the 3 -hour official hack window ; open-source libraries may be leveraged but core logic must be fresh. Any tech stack is allowed: Web, Mobile, CLI, IoT, Browser Extensions, or Game Engines . Judging criteria: Creativity (40%), Execution (30%), Entertainment & Demo (30%) . Format: Round 1: Rapid 3-Hour Prototyping Sprint The secret thematic creative constraints are revealed at the opening bell . Teams have exactly 4 hours to build and push their prototype to a public repository . Round 2: Live Stage Jury Demonstration A 5-minute live demo on stage where teams demonstrate their working quirky software to the jury. Followed by a quick 2-minute interactive Q&A session .",
